Subject: Refuse to build the AOT runtime with the debugger interface

What this does
  A release-only guard: `QJS_AOT=1` together with `JS_ENABLE_DEBUGGER=1` is a
  compile error, and the same combination is a configure error in CMake.

Why we need it
  When a debugger is attached at parse time the parser emits a trap per
  statement, and a trap changes the register bytecode and its digest. A unit
  generated from a release parse would then bind against a different program
  than the one that runs, so the mismatch must be refused at build time rather
  than surface as a missing binding.

What it adds
  `#if QJS_AOT && JS_ENABLE_DEBUGGER` -> `#error` in the engine.

Needs a bytecode version bump
  No.

diff --git a/quickjs.c b/quickjs.c
index 2370f26..d45df0f 100644
@@ -57812,6 +57812,13 @@
 #if QJS_AOT && !QJS_REGVM
 #error "QJS_AOT needs QJS_REGVM"
 #endif
+/* The parser emits a debugger trap per statement when a debugger is attached
+   at parse time, and a trap changes the register bytecode and its digest, so a
+   unit built with the interface on binds against a different program than the
+   one that runs. AOT is release-only. */
+#if QJS_AOT && JS_ENABLE_DEBUGGER
+#error "QJS_AOT cannot be combined with JS_ENABLE_DEBUGGER"
+#endif
 #if QJS_AOT_GEN && !QJS_REGVM
 #error "QJS_AOT_GEN needs QJS_REGVM"
 #endif
